{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43340716",
      "title": "Option 2: Server-side Data Fetching",
      "lectureOrder": 160,
      "videoOrder": 148,
      "sourceHash": "02843449a45f49469ebaad98f3f9c743833d522f9c1e372075e1340a8ede159d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.57,
          "end": 2.64,
          "en": "So in the previous lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.64,
          "end": 7.64,
          "en": "we used client site data fetching to load the news data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.95,
          "end": 10.59,
          "en": "And as a result, if you go to the news page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.59,
          "end": 13.08,
          "en": "and you inspect the source code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.08,
          "end": 16.44,
          "en": "you will see that in there, you see a lot of content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.44,
          "end": 20.4,
          "en": "but you won't see the actual news content here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.4,
          "end": 21.96,
          "en": "If we search for Beaver,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.96,
          "end": 24.6,
          "en": "which is part of one of the news headlines,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.6,
          "end": 26.91,
          "en": "we don't have any match in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.91,
          "end": 30.9,
          "en": "because the content that's generated on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.9,
          "end": 33.27,
          "en": "the page content that's generated there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.27,
          "end": 35.37,
          "en": "does not include those news",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.37,
          "end": 37.44,
          "en": "because we fetch them on the client side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.44,
          "end": 39.003,
          "en": "with help of useEffect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.17,
          "end": 42.15,
          "en": "Now, as you see, of course, that works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.15,
          "end": 45.3,
          "en": "but as I mentioned at the end of the last lecture already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.3,
          "end": 50.04,
          "en": "this is not the best way of fetching data when using NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.04,
          "end": 51.75,
          "en": "because even though that is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.75,
          "end": 54.48,
          "en": "how you can fetch data in any React app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.48,
          "end": 58.59,
          "en": "NextJS offers better ways of fetching data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.59,
          "end": 62.1,
          "en": "because in NextJS, all those components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.1,
          "end": 64.44,
          "en": "including all those page components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.44,
          "end": 69.44,
          "en": "as you learned by default, are React server components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.72,
          "end": 74.03999999999999,
          "en": "So React components that are meant to execute on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.03999999999999,
          "end": 75.84,
          "en": "And as it turns out,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.84,
          "end": 78.18,
          "en": "those React server components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.18,
          "end": 80.91,
          "en": "got some nice tricks up their sleeve.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.91,
          "end": 84.33,
          "en": "Most importantly, you can fetch data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.33,
          "end": 89.22,
          "en": "directly inside of them and decorate the component functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.22,
          "end": 92.343,
          "en": "with async in order to use async/await.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.42,
          "end": 95.19,
          "en": "So put in other words,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.19,
          "end": 99.3,
          "en": "React server components can return promises",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.3,
          "end": 101.46000000000001,
          "en": "instead of just JSX,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.46000000000001,
          "end": 105.18,
          "en": "and that's something traditional client side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.18,
          "end": 107.31,
          "en": "React components can't do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.31,
          "end": 110.1,
          "en": "But React server components can do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.1,
          "end": 112.62,
          "en": "And since NextJS supports them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.62,
          "end": 116.22,
          "en": "you can therefore fetch data directly inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.22,
          "end": 119.733,
          "en": "of those components when working with NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.72,
          "end": 122.67,
          "en": "Therefore, what we can do here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 122.67,
          "end": 125.58,
          "en": "is get rid of that use client directive again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.58,
          "end": 128.883,
          "en": "to convert this back to a server component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.9,
          "end": 131.253,
          "en": "get rid of useEffect here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.42,
          "end": 134.91,
          "en": "and move this code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.91,
          "end": 138.32999999999998,
          "en": "where we sent that request out of the fetch news function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.32999999999998,
          "end": 140.343,
          "en": "directly into the component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.05,
          "end": 146.38,
          "en": "We can and should now also get rid of all these states",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.42000000000002,
          "end": 149.61,
          "en": "and of all that code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 149.61,
          "end": 152.79,
          "en": "that updates those different states.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.79,
          "end": 154.89,
          "en": "I'll just keep this line of code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.89,
          "end": 157.26,
          "en": "where I parse the response data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 157.26,
          "end": 159.633,
          "en": "but I'll get rid of all that other code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161.46,
          "end": 162.293,
          "en": "That of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 162.293,
          "end": 164.28,
          "en": "also means that I'll get rid of these if checks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 164.28,
          "end": 167.46,
          "en": "and I'll show you how to still show error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 167.46,
          "end": 169.8,
          "en": "and loading fallbacks a little bit later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 169.8,
          "end": 171.35,
          "en": "For now, we'll get rid of that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 172.71,
          "end": 174.93,
          "en": "So now we have much simpler code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 174.93,
          "end": 176.67000000000002,
          "en": "and we're sending that request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 176.67000000000002,
          "end": 179.49,
          "en": "from directly inside the component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 179.49,
          "end": 181.953,
          "en": "since it's such a server component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 183.18,
          "end": 185.82,
          "en": "It's worth noting that this fetch function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 185.82,
          "end": 189.81,
          "en": "is available here, even though that code runs on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 189.81,
          "end": 193.23,
          "en": "because A, it's supported by Node.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 193.23,
          "end": 196.02,
          "en": "which executes that server side code anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 196.02,
          "end": 200.91,
          "en": "And B, NextJS extends this fetch function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 200.91,
          "end": 205.11,
          "en": "and adds some extra caching related features to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 205.11,
          "end": 207.69,
          "en": "though that's not too important here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 207.69,
          "end": 210,
          "en": "We'll take a closer look at caching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 210,
          "end": 215,
          "en": "and what NextJS does for you in the next course sections.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 215.31,
          "end": 218.13,
          "en": "So for now, it's just important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 218.13,
          "end": 219.54,
          "en": "that you can use fetch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 219.54,
          "end": 223.05,
          "en": "directly inside of a component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 223.05,
          "end": 225.24,
          "en": "Of course, now we can and should also remove the useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 225.24,
          "end": 227.703,
          "en": "and useState imports.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 229.44,
          "end": 232.8,
          "en": "Now the request could still fail,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 232.8,
          "end": 236.64,
          "en": "so I still wanna check if not response okay,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 236.64,
          "end": 239.79,
          "en": "and in that case, I'll just throw a new error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 239.79,
          "end": 242.55,
          "en": "where I'll say, failed to fetch news,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 242.55,
          "end": 245.94,
          "en": "and we'll handle that error a little bit later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 245.94,
          "end": 248.43,
          "en": "For the moment, let's focus on outputting the news.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 248.43,
          "end": 250.77,
          "en": "How would that work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 250.77,
          "end": 254.04,
          "en": "Well, we don't need to check whether they're defined or not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 254.04,
          "end": 256.98,
          "en": "because now since we have a async component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 256.98,
          "end": 260.79,
          "en": "we wait until the response data is there anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 260.79,
          "end": 264.87,
          "en": "No JSX code gets generated before that data is there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 264.87,
          "end": 268.23,
          "en": "So we won't have a scenario where news is undefined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 268.23,
          "end": 270.54,
          "en": "unless the backend returns undefined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 270.54,
          "end": 273.99,
          "en": "which my dummy backend here doesn't do though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 273.99,
          "end": 277.053,
          "en": "It always returns this array of news.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 277.89,
          "end": 280.59000000000003,
          "en": "So therefore, this check is not required anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 280.59000000000003,
          "end": 284.19,
          "en": "And hence, we can again move that news list component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 284.19,
          "end": 286.98,
          "en": "down into the returned JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 286.98,
          "end": 288.993,
          "en": "and get rid of that extra variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 290.64,
          "end": 291.69,
          "en": "And that's therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 291.69,
          "end": 295.68,
          "en": "all the code it takes when using NextJS features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 295.68,
          "end": 299.13,
          "en": "to fetch data directly on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 299.13,
          "end": 302.223,
          "en": "inside of the component function and to output it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 303.15,
          "end": 304.92,
          "en": "And therefore, now if we save that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 304.92,
          "end": 306.81,
          "en": "and reload that news page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 306.81,
          "end": 310.77,
          "en": "you see, the news data is there directly on the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 310.77,
          "end": 314.19,
          "en": "But now if we take a look at the page source code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 314.19,
          "end": 317.91,
          "en": "we will also see that all the news content is in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 317.91,
          "end": 320.493,
          "en": "So it was rendered on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 321.42,
          "end": 325.98,
          "en": "And that of course, for example, gives us an SEO advantage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 325.98,
          "end": 330,
          "en": "And hence, fetching data directly inside of the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 330,
          "end": 334.383,
          "en": "is the standard approach you should use when using NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
